This project incorporates code from the following open-source projects.
Their licence terms are reproduced in third_party/ and apply to the files named
below. Everything not named here was written for this project.

================================================================================
CoST -- Contrastive Learning of Disentangled Seasonal-Trend Representations
        for Time Series Forecasting
================================================================================
Copyright (c) 2022, Salesforce.com, Inc.
Licence: BSD 3-Clause  (third_party/LICENSE.CoST)
Source:  https://github.com/salesforce/CoST
Paper:   Gerald Woo, Chenghao Liu, Doyen Sahoo, Akshat Kumar, Steven Hoi.
         ICLR 2022.  arXiv:2202.01575

Derived files and components:
  cost.py             CoST / CoSTModel: the MoCo trend branch (momentum encoder,
                      key queue), the seasonal instance-contrastive term and the
                      encode path.
  models/losses.py    convert_coeff and the amplitude/phase seasonal loss.
  models/encoder.py   CoSTEncoder and BandedFourierLayer.
  data_processing/    the calendar-covariate construction, which follows
                      CoST's datautils._get_time_features.

All of the above are MODIFIED; README.md summarises the changes (harmonic
banding of the Fourier layer, a frequency-domain readout of the seasonal branch,
a circular phase embedding inside the loss, and the level-equivariance and
anti-collapse terms).

